(BAS-03 - keywords are case-insensitive.
 Also covers: BAS-04 (Print/print/PRINT), BAS-05 (If/if/IF), and the
 wider claim, since To/While/Increment/A NUMBER CALLED are upper-cased
 here too.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-03.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   5
   Print
   print
   PRINT
   PrInT
   If
   if
   IF
   7
   HI
)
A NUMBER CALLED x IS 5.
PRINT x.
Print "Print".
print "print".
PRINT "PRINT".
PrInT "PrInT".
If x is equal to 5 then, Print "If".
if x is equal to 5 then, Print "if".
IF x is equal to 5 then, Print "IF".
WHILE x IS LESS THAN 7, INCREMENT x.
PRINT x.
TO greet.
    PRINT "HI".

greet.
